{"id":"permutation-in-string","title":"Permutation in String","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Sliding Window","tags":["Hash Table","String","Sliding Window","Two Pointers"],"companies":{"google":2,"meta":2,"amazon":2,"microsoft":3},"description":"Given two lowercase strings `s1` and `s2`, return `true` if `s2` contains some permutation of `s1` as a **contiguous substring**, otherwise `false`.\n\nEquivalently: is there a window of `s2` of length `len(s1)` with exactly the same letter counts as `s1`?","examples":[{"input":"s1 = \"ab\", s2 = \"eidbaooo\"","output":"true","explanation":"`ba` is a permutation of `ab`."},{"input":"s1 = \"ab\", s2 = \"eidboaoo\"","output":"false","explanation":"`a` and `b` never sit next to each other."}],"constraints":["1 <= s1.length, s2.length <= 10^4","s1 and s2 consist of lowercase English letters."],"hints":["Every candidate window has the same length as s1, so this is a fixed-size sliding window.","Compare letter counts of the window with those of s1. Slide by adding the entering character and removing the leaving one.","Comparing two 26-slot arrays each step is O(26n). Track how many of the 26 counts currently match to make each step O(1)."],"function":"checkInclusion","signature":"def checkInclusion(self, s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:","arg_types":{"s1":"str","s2":"str"},"return_type":"bool","compare":"exact","tests":[{"input":{"s1":"ab","s2":"eidbaooo"},"output":true},{"input":{"s1":"ab","s2":"eidboaoo"},"output":false},{"input":{"s1":"a","s2":"a"},"output":true},{"input":{"s1":"abc","s2":"ab"},"output":false},{"input":{"s1":"adc","s2":"dcda"},"output":true},{"input":{"s1":"hello","s2":"ooolleoooleh"},"output":false},{"input":{"s1":"aab","s2":"abab"},"output":true},{"input":{"s1":"aab","s2":"abba"},"output":false},{"input":{"s1":"abc","s2":""},"output":false},{"input":{"s1":"abababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababababab","s2":""},"output":true}],"solution":"class Solution:\n    def checkInclusion(self, s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:\n        n, m = len(s1), len(s2)\n        if n > m:\n            return False\n        need = [0] * 26\n        window = [0] * 26\n        for i in range(n):\n            need[ord(s1[i]) - 97] += 1\n            window[ord(s2[i]) - 97] += 1\n        matches = sum(1 for i in range(26) if need[i] == window[i])\n        if matches == 26:\n            return True\n        for right in range(n, m):\n            # character entering the window\n            idx = ord(s2[right]) - 97\n            window[idx] += 1\n            if window[idx] == need[idx]:\n                matches += 1\n            elif window[idx] == need[idx] + 1:\n                matches -= 1\n            # character leaving the window\n            idx = ord(s2[right - n]) - 97\n            window[idx] -= 1\n            if window[idx] == need[idx]:\n                matches += 1\n            elif window[idx] == need[idx] - 1:\n                matches -= 1\n            if matches == 26:\n                return True\n        return False\n","approach":"**Fixed-size window over letter counts.** Build the count array for `s1` and for the first `len(s1)` characters of `s2`. Then slide one position at a time: increment the entering letter, decrement the leaving letter. The window is a permutation of `s1` exactly when all 26 counts agree.\n\n**O(1) per step:** instead of comparing 26 values each time, maintain `matches`, the number of letters whose count agrees. Each increment or decrement changes exactly one letter's count by one, so it can change `matches` by at most one: it becomes a match when the counts become equal, and stops being one when it moves from equal to one off. Check `matches == 26`.\n\n**Common mistakes:** forgetting the `len(s1) > len(s2)` early exit; off-by-one in which character leaves (`s2[right - n]`, not `s2[right - n - 1]`); re-sorting each window (O(n * k log k)).\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Return all starting indices instead of a boolean (Find All Anagrams in a String). Unicode alphabet (hash map plus a 'letters still mismatched' counter). Minimum window containing all characters of `s1`, order free, possibly with extras (Minimum Window Substring, a variable-size window).","complexity":{"time":"O(len(s1) + len(s2))","space":"O(1) (two 26-slot arrays)"},"similar":["valid-anagram","find-all-anagrams-in-a-string","minimum-window-substring"],"number":28,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def checkInclusion(self, s1: str, s2: str) -> bool:\n        pass\n"}